SM(191,{"n":"Ephesians 1.1-14","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Ephesians 1.1-14.mp3","d":2813.7,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.16,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.88,"We'll go ahead and uh start with in uh St."],[24.88,"Paul's Epistle to the Ephesians uh chapter one verse one."],[31.52,"Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God, to the saints who are in Ephesus and faithful in Christ Jesus."],[40.96,"So uh I already mentioned about the in Ephesus."],[45.6,"Um and uh it's also worth noting, one more footnote on that."],[51.36,"If you go and look up what the church fathers, if you look at their commentaries on Ephesus, when they comment on this verse, a lot of them leave out the in Ephesus."],[60.44,"They at least don't comment on it."],[63.0,"I don't know if that's because they didn't have it in their copy yet, or if they knew it was some kind of heading."],[69.58,"Like they never, they don't really say anything about about Ephesus in this."],[73.66,"They just talk about, they say, well, St."],[76.06,"Paul identifies the recipients as the saints, as the holy ones, as being faithful holy ones, and as being uh faithful in Christ Jesus."],[88.7,"So we've talked a lot in St."],[93.74,"Paul's epistles that we've already been through about his apostleship."],[96.56,"So he's saying he's one sent by Jesus Christ, by the will of God, God there being God the Father."],[101.92,"God the Father. Christ"],[104.21,"And so there's this order."],[109.31,"Christ has sent Saint Paul."],[112.03,"And so he's writing with that authority."],[116.11,"That's gonna be paralleled."],[117.55,"I'll go ahead and read verse two."],[118.67,"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."],[124.27,"Look at that closely."],[125.55,"Saint Paul is speaking for God the Father and for our Lord Jesus Christ."],[131.63,"When he says grace to you and peace."],[133.71,"So that's the parallel to what he says in verse 1."],[136.67,"There's God the Father, Christ sends Paul."],[140.43,"St. Paul says, I'm here speaking to you from them."],[147.31,"And they they uh say to you grace and and peace."],[154.07,"We've talked before about the word that's translated saints, i.e. which uh the modern pronunciation of Greek makes that word sound so weird."],[163.67,"It's like all vowels, but um it means holy ones."],[169.21,"And this is the this was the word that was used to refer to uh angels, angelic beings in the Old Testament."],[177.21,"We talked about this at the beginning of 1 Corinthians."],[180.7,"And so um saints, holy ones is a status."],[187.04,"It's a status that they have, and then their faithfulness."],[192.69,"Their faithfulness to Christ is sort of what constitutes that status."],[199.97,"They are God's holy ones because they are faithful to Jesus Christ."],[205.57,"And the reason I'm breaking this down is remember, right at the beginning of St."],[209.89,"Paul's epistles, he sort of lays out his themes for the rest of the letter."],[215.57,"So we're already here, this introduction starting to get starting to get some of those themes."],[222.53,"So they have this status as holy ones of God because of their faithfulness, their faithfulness to Christ."],[234.61,"Verse 3: Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly places in Christ."],[247.21,"So he blesses, notice it's the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ."],[255.93,"We've talked before."],[257.21,"I don't know how much to go into this now, but we've talked before about how this language does occur in the Bible."],[263.29,"That the Father is Christ's God."],[268.99,"Notice he uses the name Jesus here."],[271.63,"We've mentioned that when St."],[272.91,"Paul uses the term Jesus and not just Christ, because most of the time he just says Christ."],[277.31,"When he says Christ Jesus or Jesus Christ, he's referring to the incarnate Christ."],[283.77,"That the Father is his God."],[286.01,"As Christ said before, ascended, I'm going to my Father and your Father, my God and your God."],[294.11,"Because when God the Son becomes incarnate, he's not an atheist."],[301.31,"Still believes it is Father."],[306.83,"Okay, and notice the Father has blessed us with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly places in Christ."],[318.27,"Okay So when he says he's blessed us with every blessing, he's not talking about our bank account and our job and our success."],[330.52,"The way a lot of folks in America talk about blessings, today."],[335.17,"These are every blessing in the heavenly places."],[338.53,"You say, well, wait a second."],[341.09,"Last I looked around."],[342.53,"I mean, Louisiana is heavenly."],[344.77,"Not when it's 82 degrees at the end of October."],[348.61,"But you could say, hey, I used to live in West Virginia."],[352.21,"They say that's almost heaven."],[354.26,"But that's not talking about Ephesus."],[358.02,"That's not talking about uh their hometown being a heavenly place."],[364.2,"This is going back to that theme."],[365.8,"He's already called them holy ones."],[370.62,"So part of that status of holy ones, is God the Father having exalted them to this heavenly place in this heavenly position."],[382.77,"So this is already true of them in some sense."],[387.41,"This is already true of them in some sense."],[391.33,"And he's done this in Christ."],[394.05,"So it's in Christ that they've been placed in this position."],[400.53,"Verse 4. Just as he chose us in him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blame before him in love."],[413.29,"Okay. Now, we're in Ephesians 1."],[418.09,"So I know when we went through Galatians, it seemed like I just kept picking on poor Martin Luther."],[424.09,"Well, he's going to get a break, and I'm going to pick on my old friend John Calvin for a while while we're in the first couple chapter couple chapters of Ephesians."],[433.69,"Okay. So, on first read, if you're familiar, even vaguely, with predestination and Calvinism, you might say, Well, he chose us in him."],[445.23,"So God the Father chose us in Christ before the foundation of the world."],[451.17,"Before the world was founded."],[452.93,"Okay. So this is so the question though that we have to ask in order to understand this is who is us."],[467.02,"And is it and if there's an us, then there's a them."],[473.15,"So who's us and who's them?"],[478.19,"Okay. So to take the Calvinist interpretation of this, you would say, well, us, is everyone in the history of the world who will ever have faith."],[494.4,"Okay. And them is everyone in the history of the world who won't."],[501.16,"Okay? Have we seen anything in Ephesians so far that would give you those two categories?"],[510.84,"Faith hasn't been there."],[512.42,"Faithfulness. So you're having to sort of create those categories."],[523.6,"So if we just go with categories that Saint Paul has already used."],[531.24,"Us is the saints."],[537.89,"Us is the people who have that status."],[540.05,"That would have been my guess, but I was"],[542.49,"Right? So he chose, for people to have that status."],[551.02,"Okay? As opposed to that them would be people who don't have that status."],[558.0,"Or may not have that status."],[560.0,"And we don't even know how big or I mean them could be an empty set in this case."],[566.18,"Us could be everybody."],[568.18,"Us could be every human."],[571.06,"Hypothetically, as we're reading here."],[574.49,"Because St. Paul doesn't say."],[576.17,"We just know us includes St."],[577.85,"Paul and the people he's writing to."],[580.51,"We know that for sure."],[581.55,"And he's saying this about them"],[585.66,"And so God makes this choice."],[590.22,"He does it before the foundation of the world."],[593.5,"Okay. This phrase foundation, literally means like a building foundation."],[604.84,"Before the foundation of the world."],[608.36,"So what St."],[610.2,"Paul is saying here is that before he chose to create everything."],[621.22,"Before God the Father chose to create. everything"],[632.15,"Holy ones of God in the heavenly places."],[634.95,"But as of humans."],[638.39,"So that's a specified group of humans."],[641.45,"Meaning the purpose."],[644.17,"Because it's before."],[645.59,"This isn't talking about God is like sitting there going, okay, well, I think I want to do this."],[652.31,"And then later on he says, you know what?"],[653.83,"I think I'm going to create a world."],[655.68,"These are connected for St."],[657.44,"Paul. So the purpose for which God creates the world is to do this for us."],[665.97,"So St Okay."],[669.69,"Wow. Paul is not in any way defining us."],[674.57,"Who is us, who isn't us here."],[679.34,"Or at least he's not excluding anyone from us."],[681.58,"He's including some people in us, but he hasn't excluded anybody."],[684.54,"We know it's a category of humans, though."],[686.52,"Yeah. Because it includes Paul and the people he's writing to who are all humans."],[690.82,"Yeah. So could it include angels too?"],[694.98,"Well, he's not writing to angels, so we don't know."],[697.07,"And angels are already angels."],[698.67,"Right. So they're already the holy ones of God."],[703.79,"So St. Paul is not making any point whatsoever. about who is and isn't in the us"],[713.09,"He's making no argument about that."],[715.89,"So there's nothing in here about predestination or election."],[719.33,"He's making a point about the fact that the glorification of human persons was the purpose for which God created the world."],[735.03,"He made the same point back in Romans."],[737.59,"This is another one of those."],[739.59,"Hey, he's saying the same thing he said in Romans."],[741.99,"And we're gonna see as he goes on, he's gonna say the same thing he said in Galatians 3, too."],[746.15,"So there's no reason to think this wasn't St."],[748.39,"Paul. He's talking about the same stuff."],[750.2,"But so that's the point he's making."],[751.24,"'s making. He this causal point"],[755.34,"That the glorification of human persons in Christ."],[759.44,"Then receiving this status in Christ as holy ones in the heavenly places is the purpose for which God laid the foundation, began, and created the world."],[777.2,"Alright, and he did that so that we should be holy."],[780.9,"Holy ones, without blame before him."],[784.28,"Purified of our sins."],[787.64,"And in love."],[789.17,"haring S sharing his love with us."],[793.85,"Verse 5. Having predestined us, here we go again"],[800.13,"Our friend John is getting triggered."],[803.41,"Having predestined us to adoption adoption as sons by Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will."],[817.89,"What have we said before?"],[819.17,"Predestined means, actually, in the Greek word."],[823.09,"Set things in order in advance."],[825.49,"Set things in order in advance."],[827.33,"Okay. He arranged things in advance."],[832.8,"This is part of his, this is parallel to."],[834.98,"He creates the world."],[837.06,"His purpose is the glorification, of human persons, that they be holy ones, that they be blameless before him, that they share in his love, and so he creates the world, and in creating the world, he sets everything in order for humans to receive adoption as sons, to become sons of God."],[863.49,"Sons of God, another Old Testament term for angels."],[867.43,"This is parallel to the holy ones."],[869.29,"So that we would receive in Christ again."],[874.49,"Receive adoption as sons."],[878.33,"Okay? According to the good pleasure of his will."],[883.27,"Meaning he sons."],[886.31,"Adoption of sons by Jesus Christ, according to his will."],[890.95,"So it's by means of Christ."],[893.51,"By means of Christ."],[894.65,"Not sons of Christ."],[897.61,"Sons of Christ as distinct from sons of God."],[900.81,"No, we're sons of God by adoption."],[904.01,"Christ is the Son of God."],[908.65,"Begotten. As opposed to us, who are adopted."],[913.5,"And we're adopted through him."],[915.34,"His sonship, is what is the basis for our receiving this adopted sonship."],[922.56,"And he does this according to the good pleasure of his will"],[929.0,"Because God desired to do good to us because he loves humanity."],[932.76,"He was his will to do all his best and just saying."],[935.74,"Yeah. Out of his good pleasure, but his desire to do good to human beings, out of his love for us."],[944.62,"To the praise of the glory of his grace, by which he made us accepted in the beloved."],[957.62,"So that what they translate, the glory of his grace should is really more like his glorious grace."],[966.38,"But the the idea is that God has given this to us freely."],[972.48,"We didn't earn adoption as sons and all that."],[975.68,"Alright, he created the world to do this."],[977.52,"Obviously, we didn't exist yet when he made this decision to do all this for us."],[985.16,"And so we now respond in praise for what this great thing he has done for us in creating us and creating this world and in doing it in such a way that we have this destiny set before us."],[999.78,"In Christ. Christ. So I'm referring to"],[1003.3,"Right. We're accepted into God's family in Christ."],[1009.32,"So none of this, none of this for St."],[1011.08,"Paul is apart from Christ"],[1014.82,"As he's gonna say in another epistle, there's one mediator between God the Father and man, the man Christ Jesus."],[1025.01,"So Christ is the means, of our adoption."],[1030.07,"It's St. Athanasius famously put it, God became man so that men might become gods."],[1036.77,"Sons of God."],[1038.77,"So this is he's he's just reading what St."],[1041.49,"Paul is saying here."],[1043.19,"Okay. So notice there's nothing in those verses we just read, even though every Calvinist I know, and I know quite a few can quote these verses to you by heart."],[1056.11,"There's nothing in there that says anything about God having picked some people to go to heaven and some people to go to hell before he created the world."],[1066.97,"It just doesn't say that."],[1070.1,"It doesn't say that."],[1071.38,"You have to read these categories into the text."],[1074.5,"St. Paul doesn't say it."],[1076.9,"Okay. And what St."],[1078.34,"Paul is saying here is very consistent with what he says in Galatians 3, what he says in Romans 8."],[1084.92,"We can go back and we're not going to do that right now, but you can go back and read through those."],[1089.8,"You'll see he's using the same language about becoming sons of God in Romans 8, about uh all of creation groaning like a woman about to give birth to produce the sons of God."],[1095.8,"This is the purpose of creation"],[1102.94,"This is consistent Pauline theology."],[1105.58,"This is what we call theosis in the Orthodox Church."],[1110.03,"This is this is what St."],[1111.95,"Paul is talking about."],[1113.65,"So he's saying, this is how he's beginning his letter to these folks."],[1118.53,"We saw how he used some similar language, the language of holy ones with the church in Corinth at the beginning of 1 Corinthians."],[1126.21,"Because remember, he was having to call them to repentance."],[1128.45,"He's trying to remind them this is this is who you are in Christ."],[1132.21,"Start acting like it."],[1133.85,"Like start start being the person who, you know, who. uh you've been made in in Christ"],[1141.41,"So here he's reminding them, he's laying out, you know, this is the gospel."],[1145.27,"Here's who you are."],[1146.87,"Here's the status you have in Christ."],[1150.33,"And you have it not because, you know, like Julius Caesar, you were just such a great man that you experienced apotheosis at your death and mounted up to heaven and became a god."],[1163.13,"No. God create loved you before the world was created."],[1167.5,"He created the world in order to, you know, give you this destiny and this status that you've received in him, adoption into his family."],[1178.08,"Becoming an heir of his promises."],[1180.45,"All of this has been given to you, and this is who you are now."],[1181.17,"Paul is starting in writing to them"],[1184.75,"That's where St."],[1188.43,"So this is what he wants them to have in mind."],[1191.07,"This is who you are, who I'm writing to."],[1194.11,"Even though you may not look like it, you may not feel like it, you may not act like it on any given day."],[1199.15,"This is who you actually are in Christ and how important you are, and what the love of God means, you know, for each of you."],[1207.87,"Even if you're peasants doing glorified slave labor in a field all day, somewhere in the Lycus Valley."],[1216.45,"And you're you're a peasant and you're a nobody."],[1219.59,"In terms of the Roman government, you're a slave, you're a woman."],[1223.69,"Whatever that society held no value for."],[1224.57,"This is who you are in Christ"],[1226.45,"This is the value that God has for you."],[1231.25,"Who I'm writing to, every single one of you."],[1236.93,"Verse 7. In him we have redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of sins according to the riches of his grace."],[1247.97,"Okay. So let's pause there."],[1251.57,"Okay, redemption through his blood."],[1253.25,"Remember, redemption is to buy back."],[1258.17,"Or to uh, you know, if you redeem a coupon or you redeem a gift certificate."],[1264.71,"You go, you turn it in, and you get something right back."],[1271.2,"And so Christ offered something and got us."],[1276.58,"In this case it's his blood."],[1280.28,"So Christ offers himself, in order to get us back."],[1286.61,"I'm curious how I sure haven't read the whole thing, but I thought it was unusual that he used the term the beloved."],[1298.13,"Yeah. It sounds like Ruby."],[1301.65,"Oh. Is that special?"],[1306.45,"Well, he's um he just talked about um in verse four."],[1315.55,"That we'd be without blame before him in love."],[1320.24,"Talk about us."],[1322.21,"And one of his themes all through those sort of nested verses is that everything we receive from God we receive in Christ."],[1328.69,"So one of his themes in all of these nested verses is that everything we receive from God the Father, we receive in and through Christ."],[1339.51,"And that includes the love of God, because Christ is the beloved capital B."],[1347.11,"Okay. The love between the persons of the Trinity is infinite and goes back into eternity."],[1353.8,"And it's that love that's then shared with us as humans."],[1360.14,"So God is sharing his life with us."],[1362.94,"When we're adopted, become adopted sons of God, God is sharing his his life and his love that has eternally existed between the the three persons of the Trinity with us."],[1380.3,"So is that something that you would find elsewhere?"],[1384.46,"Yeah. Yeah. Yeah."],[1391.9,"Okay, so we have we have redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of sins, according to the ri.ches of his grace"],[1400.02,"Okay, so what's the connection between blood and the forgiveness of sins?"],[1405.46,"Well, like in the Old Testament, what's a it would kill a lamb and cleanse the temple with a blood."],[1411.14,"You were well, yeah."],[1413.94,"Yeah. I was about to correct you, but I may not need to."],[1416.5,"I'll give you the benefit of the doubt."],[1419.23,"So the point we need to make is that in sacrifices, killing the animal was irrelevant."],[1428.38,"Killing the animal is not ritualized."],[1431.42,"It is not a significant ritual moment."],[1434.06,"It does not have ritual meaning."],[1437.5,"You can go all through the Torah."],[1440.3,"There's nothing in there about how to kill the animal you sacrifice."],[1441.5,"Because sacrifices are sacred meals"],[1447.09,"They all involve food."],[1448.77,"If you're going to eat an animal, you have to kill it first."],[1452.98,"You're not going to eat it alive."],[1455.38,"There were some pagan rituals where they did that, so I shouldn't say you have to."],[1458.74,"But in the Torah, yeah, because you're not going to eat blood."],[1462.74,"You're not going to eat animal with the blood in it."],[1464.26,"You have to kill it and drain the blood."],[1466.88,"But that's incidental to eating it."],[1470.66,"There are all kinds of instructions in the Torah about how to butcher it."],[1475.3,"And how and what parts to eat and what parts not to eat, and what parts to burn and offer to God, and what parts and what to do with what part."],[1482.47,"Nothing about how to kill it."],[1483.59,"Dividing up the parts"],[1484.83,"You're using butcher in the sense of what the butcher is."],[1491.07,"Yeah. Yeah. How to cut it up and separate it and yeah, yeah, yeah."],[1495.63,"Do all the cuts."],[1496.75,"Yeah. That's all ritualized."],[1499.73,"But killing the animal isn't."],[1501.33,"So this this isn't blood is not a stand in for death."],[1509.81,"So he's not saying we have forgiveness of sins because Christ died."],[1515.33,"Christ's death is significant."],[1517.07,"And we've seen several places, like 1 Corinthians 15, where he where he talks about that."],[1520.75,"But in this case, when he talks about blood, that's not talking about Christ's death."],[1526.67,"That's talking about what was done with the blood from a sacrifice, which they didn't eat."],[1527.87,"They did not eat the blood"],[1536.61,"The blood was used to wipe away the taint of sin."],[1542.53,"It was used to purify, to cover, to wipe away sin."],[1547.17,"It was seen to sort of absorb, the sin residue, the goo."],[1554.4,"Because you have in the sacrificial system, you have guilt offerings and sin offerings that are happening literally every day."],[1566.5,"So then why do you need a day of atonement?"],[1571.26,"For the good temples, for adultery."],[1573.98,"For the well, yeah, you're atoning on the Day of Atonement for the physical objects in the tabernacle."],[1580.78,"Well, the physical objects didn't do anything."],[1582.62,"The blessed, because the sin taints everything around it."],[1585.1,"Because the sin taints everything around it."],[1586.62,"It taints the ground, it taints the world around it, there's this residue."],[1591.02,"That's gotta be purified."],[1592.38,"That's what's purified in it."],[1594.14,"That's what atonement is."],[1597.1,"Is that purification?"],[1598.7,"Okay, so when when he talks about Christ's blood in terms of the forgiveness of sins, that's the imagery."],[1605.92,"We're gonna see this in other epistles."],[1607.28,"We're gonna see this in St."],[1608.0,"John's epistles especially."],[1609.28,"He talks about Christ's blood purifying us and washing us."],[1612.5,"This idea of washing something in blood is kind of counterintuitive."],[1617.71,"But it's because of this idea of the blood as purifying."],[1625.47,"Okay. So he's talking about Christ, we're we're uh redeemed, by Christ."],[1632.88,"We're brought back, from death."],[1636.82,"And we're purified."],[1639.38,"We're purified of our sins through his blood."],[1645.46,"And he does this according to the riches of his grace, meaning God's doing this again."],[1650.74,"He hasn't stopped talking about the stuff God does."],[1653.16,"So we started out with God the Father."],[1657.02,"And the creation of the world, for this purpose of our adoption as sons."],[1662.55,"Now he's talking about what Christ has done, for us."],[1667.49,"Redeeming us, purifying us from sin, which is all prerequisite to us receiving that status and that adoption."],[1678.69,"Verse 8, which he made to abound toward us, his grace, in all wisdom and prudence, having made known to us the mystery of his will, according to his good pleasure, which he purposed in himself."],[1693.21,"Hey, what does that mean?"],[1694.81,"Well, this plan."],[1697.95,"The plan of redemption in Christ, the plan of uh our adoption as sons."],[1706.17,"Our glorification, isn't something that shows up on the first page of scripture."],[1712.51,"God doesn't come to Adam and say, okay, here's how this is all going to go down."],[1716.44,"It's gonna take several millennia, but I'll just fill you in now."],[1720.82,"It's not all laid out to Abraham."],[1724.0,"The broad strokes are given."],[1727.25,"But it's still a mystery."],[1728.87,"How it's uh it's not all laid out to Moses, it's not all laid out to Isaiah, it's not right."],[1734.95,"But to us, made known to us, again, us is Saint Paul and the people he's writing to."],[1741.76,"He's not necessarily excluding anybody"],[1746.26,"So it made known to us this plan."],[1749.88,"All of this that God has done for us."],[1752.14,"The gospel has now been made known to us, again, according to his good pleasure, which he purposed in himself."],[1760.72,"He gave it to Saint Paul, the gospel, Saint Paul preached it to them."],[1765.61,"And it's spreading throughout the world."],[1768.17,"So it's now in this time when Saint Paul is writing that all of this has been revealed."],[1774.43,"The mystery that was true all along."],[1776.99,"God purposed all this, remember, according to his good pleasure, the same terms he uses here before the foundation of the world."],[1784.45,"And now it's been, now we're at the point in his plan where he's revealing it."],[1790.23,"So Saint Paul again sees the change that happens to him on the road to Damascus as a change in time where he is on the timeline."],[1801.29,"From expecting it to now this has arrived."],[1804.5,"Now it's been revealed."],[1806.18,"Now God has shown it to us."],[1810.74,"That in the dispensation of the fullness of the times, he might gather together in one all things in Christ, both which are in heaven and which are on earth."],[1823.3,"Okay. So for Saint Paul, now the whole purpose of God is now coming to its fulfillment."],[1836.91,"In the communities that he's starting, in the gospel that he's preaching."],[1842.77,"That this isn't just, again, oh hey, I've got a new religion, guys."],[1848.05,"It's better than the old one."],[1850.05,"You can eat pork now."],[1854.98,"It's not a new exact saying, I'm coming offer you a new religious system."],[1858.98,"It's better than you're not gonna have to kill animals anymore."],[1862.52,"You're gonna be able to do it anywhere, you're not gonna have to go to Jerusalem."],[1866.72,"St. Paul sees this as a shift in epoch."],[1870.5,"Now is the time where the heavens and the earth, this whole creation, because God created everything for this purpose."],[1877.46,"Now that this purpose is being fulfilled, the whole purpose of the creation is being fulfilled."],[1884.63,"So to put more more uh fine point on it, he's saying this is the end times."],[1891.21,"This is where it's all coming together."],[1894.35,"Everything is now coming together in Christ."],[1897.72,"Why is he reiterating this to them?"],[1900.36,"Because some of the people he's writing to are essentially slaves doing farm work for 12 to 16 hours a day for enough food to survive with their families."],[1915.06,"They're women, they're slaves, they're people who are disrespected, looked down upon, poor, and he's saying, yeah, but here's where you are in the cosmos."],[1926.44,"The God who created everything created it for you because he loves you."],[1934.04,"And once again, to reiterate, is St."],[1936.92,"Paul excluding anyone from this us yet?"],[1943.46,"He has yet to exclude anyone from this us."],[1947.14,"So again, there's no Calvinist version of predestination here."],[1952.58,"There's no them yet, as opposed to the us."],[1960.94,"Verse 11, in him also we have obtained an inheritance."],[1966.62,"There's that language again from Galatians 3 with the sons of God and the inheritance in Romans 8."],[1972.75,"St. Paul's always using in him we have obtained an inheritance."],[1976.67,"Because as he said in Galatians, Christ is the heir, he's the Son."],[1980.99,"We've received adopted sonship, as he just reiterated, and that means we receive in Christ a part of the inheritance."],[1991.71,"Being predestined according to the purpose of him who works all things according to the counsel of his will. that we who first trusted in Christ should be to the praise of his glory"],[2004.71,"Okay, there's fun with translations."],[2008.47,"Okay. Um, again, the inheritance."],[2016.24,"What's predestined here?"],[2019.04,"Arranged. Arranged before."],[2021.84,"But but what is it that was predestined?"],[2024.72,"It's the inheritance."],[2028.91,"The inheritance is predestined."],[2031.65,"Again, this was all set up by God out of his love, out of his goodwill toward us."],[2039.54,"Um, that we would receive it."],[2043.51,"And he works all things according to the counsel of his will."],[2047.69,"Meaning he didn't just draw up a big blueprint, he didn't get a big bulletin board with a whole bunch of strings and pins."],[2055.71,"Here's how it's all gonna go down."],[2058.08,"But that God has been active."],[2061.54,"All the way through, from the creation of the world until right then."],[2066.27,"To make all of these things happen."],[2068.85,"To bring all of these things to fruition."],[2071.25,"God's been working this whole time."],[2074.55,"Not sitting somewhere planning it out, not puppet master."],[2078.21,"But he's been actively working."],[2079.97,"ing To br all of these things to fruition."],[2080.29,"All this grace St"],[2083.43,"Because that's what his grace is, remember?"],[2087.43,"Paul was talking about is the same thing."],[2088.95,"Grace is God acting in his creation."],[2092.71,"He's been doing it the whole time."],[2095.55,"With the purpose of our glorification, our receiving an inheritance, our being adopted as sons of God."],[2104.77,"Our receiving the blessing in the heavenly places."],[2109.83,"That's the purpose."],[2111.11,"And again, no one's been excluded."],[2118.23,"So that this should be more like we who in the first place trusted in Christ should be to the praise of his glory."],[2132.03,"Saying at the beginning, we trusted in Christ."],[2138.96,"We began this life of faithfulness."],[2141.44,"And God is continuing to work to bring to fruition."],[2145.28,"God's just not just working at the macro level in the cosmos, to bring it to fruition."],[2153.06,"He's working in your and my life, in that peasant's life, in that slave's life in the Roman world, to bring them from the point of trusting in Christ, hearing the gospel, to glory for the praise of God."],[2176.51,"So he's active in the whole world, he's active in your individual life."],[2182.64,"To bring this plan conceived out of his love to fruition."],[2188.96,"No one excluded yet."],[2192.72,"This is true of St."],[2194.64,"Paul and everyone he's speaking to."],[2201.04,"Doesn't mean it's true of every single human who ever existed, because that's not what St."],[2205.12,"Paul's talking about."],[2206.58,"We know it's true of St."],[2208.34,"Paul and the people he's talking to."],[2210.34,"So, verse 13."],[2212.86,"In him you also trusted."],[2215.9,"Even though you notice trusted is in italics."],[2219.26,"In him you also, but he just said, We who first, and now we you."],[2224.84,"Uh, you also trusted, after you heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation, in whom also, having believed, you were sealed with the Holy Spirit of promise."],[2238.2,"Okay. So, St."],[2241.24,"Paul received the gospel."],[2244.41,"And so God is now working through, as he said all the way back in verse 1, God is working through Saint Paul to bring the gospel to them."],[2252.74,"They hear the gospel of their salvation."],[2253.46,"the gospel. Now remember what is"],[2258.38,"The gospel is not here's what you need to do to be saved."],[2263.67,"When Saint Paul or anyone else, any of the other apostles in the book of Acts, preach the gospel to somebody, they respond by saying, What must I do to be saved?"],[2274.39,"So if that's what the gospel was, it would be a dumb question."],[2277.83,"They'd be asking the apostle to repeat themselves."],[2282.23,"So that can't be what it was."],[2284.05,"What we see when they preach the gospel, remember, Evangelion in uh Greek in the singular, is what's used for gospel in the New Testament."],[2295.97,"It was more commonly used in the Roman world. in the plural evangelia"],[2299.93,"It was the report of the victory, military victories, usually, but victories and accomplishments of an emperor or a general or a senator or a prominent figure."],[2322.33,"Which is what he was just talking about."],[2325.45,"Their redemption, the forgiveness of their sins."],[2329.63,"This is what Christ accomplished."],[2331.87,"They heard about it and they trusted in it."],[2336.73,"When they heard it and trusted in it, they were baptized."],[2342.77,"And they received the Holy Spirit."],[2348.69,"They were sealed with the Holy Spirit of promise."],[2352.21,"Okay, we're gonna talk about the of promise in just a second in the next verse."],[2356.34,"Sealed. And we still say this when we charismate someone after baptism."],[2360.34,"We say the seal of the gift of the Holy Spirit."],[2362.5,"Everybody says seal."],[2365.14,"Okay. So a seal, the seal we're talking about, is not shrink wrap."],[2374.72,"'s it It's a seal, like a wax seal."],[2378.28,"Put your stamp on it"],[2381.56,"Right. Put your stamp on it."],[2383.62,"So you were stamped."],[2384.58,"ed You were claim."],[2384.74,"Okay Now, again."],[2394.08,"I probably shouldn't even."],[2395.52,"I feel disingenuous saying I hate to pick on John Calvin."],[2399.36,"Because I don't, honestly."],[2402.56,"But I I'm going to."],[2405.04,"Okay. So notice if you put a wax seal on something, that seal can be broken."],[2414.66,"Yeah, yeah. So some of our Calvinist friends will come to us and read this verse and say, Well, look, you're sealed with the Holy Spirit."],[2425.54,"That means you can never fall away, you can never lose the Holy Spirit."],[2431.2,"Because they've already misread all these verses we just read to say that God picked you as opposed to other people, which is nowhere in there."],[2438.93,"We all agree."],[2440.13,"It's just not there."],[2441.35,"And so they say, Well, see, he picked you, and he saved you as a gift that he didn't give to everybody, he just gave to you."],[2450.47,"And so now look, you're sealed, and that means, you know, it's permanent."],[2457.13,"But anybody who knew anything about wax seals knew they could be broken."],[2465.22,"Sort of the whole point of them was that they would break easily, so you could tell if it had been opened."],[2469.78,"Yeah. They weren't intended to be a permanent, unbreakable"],[2477.5,"St. Paul could have said that if that's what he meant."],[2479.98,"He could have said in which you were bound."],[2482.4,"Or in which you were right."],[2483.84,"He could have made it like a permanent."],[2485.92,"There are ways to, you know, he could have just said an eternal seal."],[2490.96,"An unbreakable seal."],[2493.12,"He doesn't say that."],[2494.0,"You were sealed."],[2497.12,"He doesn't say whether it can or can't be broken."],[2501.42,"But the analogy of a wax seal would lead one to believe that it's possible to break it."],[2508.7,"Okay. But so you were sealed, you were marked, you were stamped."],[2514.98,"And he says that the Holy Spirit is the spirit of promise, because, verse 14, who, the Holy Spirit, is the guarantee of our inheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession to the praise of his glory."],[2532.48,"So, again, sometimes our Calvinist friends will want to read a lot into that English word guarantee."],[2540.56,"Okay? But that's taking a modern definition of guarantee."],[2546.82,"This is the earlier, it's the new King James, but it's not that new."],[2550.74,"Uh, this is the earlier mention of guarantee, which basically meant deposit."],[2557.08,"You give someone a guarantee, meaning you give someone a deposit as evidence that you are going to come and pay the rest."],[2565.16,"Oh, yeah. So the Holy Spirit is the guarantee of our inheritance, meaning like the down payment."],[2573.19,"The deposit of our inheritance."],[2577.88,"And it serves then as a guarantee until the redemption."],[2584.38,"You turn it, cash it in."],[2586.36,"The redemption of the purchased possession, in which case, we're in this case, we're talking about the inheritance. to the praise of his glory"],[2599.5,"So this inheritance, being adopted as sons of God, our glorification in the heavenly places, all of these things he's talked about."],[2608.54,"The down payment on that is the Holy Spirit who is given to you at your baptism."],[2614.96,"When you first trusted, trusted in the gospel you heard of how Christ had accomplished your salvation."],[2623.25,"You were sealed and marked, and you were given the Holy Spirit as a down payment."],[2628.75,"As a deposit."],[2629.87,"That means that the Holy Spirit."],[2633.09,"Holy Spirit, who's God Himself."],[2636.1,"God indwelling us is the the beginning represents beginning of our glorification."],[2639.14,"beginning. The of our inheritance"],[2646.28,"It's not disassociated."],[2648.57,"It's not a coupon or a ticket."],[2650.17,"It's a deposit."],[2652.01,"It's part of the inheritance."],[2655.13,"Okay. So we become temple of the Holy Spirit."],[2658.01,"Now again, none of this language says, well, if you've got the deposit, you are automatically going to redeem the whole inheritance."],[2672.01,"There wouldn't be a need for a deposit."],[2676.09,"You can default a loan still"],[2678.73,"You could default on a loan."],[2680.57,"Yeah. You could lose your deposit."],[2682.73,"Okay You could break a seal."],[2689.65,"So I'm not saying that St."],[2691.25,"Paul is saying, hey, this seal could be broken."],[2695.17,"Hey, you might not get, you're not necessarily going to get the inheritance."],[2699.65,"He's not making that point."],[2702.29,"I just, because of our Calvinist friends, have to make the point that he isn't making the opposite point either."],[2709.23,"He's not saying anything about just like he didn't say anything about anyone being excluded from the inheritance."],[2717.25,"And from God's grace and from adoption."],[2719.89,"He didn't make any mention of anyone being excluded."],[2722.54,"He's here not making any mention of this being unbreakable or impossible."],[2730.44,"He said that God is working to bring it all through to a conclusion."],[2736.12,"But he hasn't said anything here about whether we can, you know, decide not to bring it to conclusion."],[2749.29,"Because all the way back at the beginning, remember, it was the saints of God, the holy ones of God, who are faithful to Christ."],[2760.09,"Faithful is an ongoing verb and action."],[2767.47,"You first trusted, and then you're faithful."],[2769.87,"Over time God and and the guarantee, the promise here is God is doing his part."],[2780.36,"God started doing his part before there was a world."],[2783.72,"God started doing his part before creation for my salvation and your salvation."],[2792.68,"But he hasn't given any guarantees about our faithfulness."],[2798.77,"Which is the other piece of that."],[2800.93,"And which he's going to delve into as we go on."],[2803.89,"But this is probably a good place to pause, even though we're not at the end of the chapter."],[2808.85,"Largely because, as you'll see in the next verse, he starts with a therefore."],[2812.69,"So thank you, everybody."]],"o":[{"t":20.88,"lv":2,"h":"Ephesians 1:1 - Paul, apostle; \"in Ephesus\" again","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:1</b> \"Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God, to the saints who are in Ephesus and faithful in Christ Jesus\"</li><li class=\"d0\">One more footnote on <b>\"in Ephesus\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">church fathers' commentaries on this verse: many <b>leave it out</b>, or at least don't comment on it</li><li class=\"d1\">\"don't know\" if their copy lacked it, or they saw it as <b>some kind of heading</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they just say Paul identifies the recipients as <b>the saints, holy ones, faithful in Christ Jesus</b></li></ul>"},{"t":88.7,"lv":3,"h":"Apostleship; 1:2 grace and peace","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Already covered his <b>apostleship</b> in earlier epistles</li><li class=\"d1\">sent by <b>Jesus Christ</b>, by the will of <b>God</b> = God the <b>Father</b></li><li class=\"d1\">an <b>order</b>: Father -> Christ -> Christ sends Paul -> he writes with that <b>authority</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:2</b> \"grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ\" - \"look at that closely\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>parallel</b> to v. 1: Paul speaks <b>for</b> the Father and Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">Father, Christ sends Paul, Paul: \"I'm here speaking to you <b>from them</b>\" - they say \"grace and peace\"</li></ul>"},{"t":154.07,"lv":3,"h":"\"Saints\" = holy ones","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Word translated <b>saints</b> - modern Greek pronunciation sounds weird, \"all vowels\"</li><li class=\"d1\">means <b>holy ones</b></li><li class=\"d1\">OT word for <b>angels, angelic beings</b> - from the start of <b>1 Corinthians</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Holy ones = a <b>status</b></li><li class=\"d1\">their <b>faithfulness</b> to Christ \"constitutes that status\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God's holy ones <b>because</b> faithful to Jesus Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul lays out his <b>themes</b> at the start of his epistles -> here already</li></ul>"},{"t":234.61,"lv":2,"h":"1:3 - Blessed be the God and Father","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:3</b> \"blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us with <b>every spiritual blessing in the heavenly places</b> in Christ\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ\" - <b>the Father is Christ's God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul says <b>Jesus</b> / <b>Christ Jesus</b> / <b>Jesus Christ</b> (not just \"Christ\") = the <b>incarnate</b> Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ: \"I'm going to my Father and your Father, <b>my God and your God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"when God the Son becomes incarnate, he's <b>not an atheist</b>\" - still believes in his Father</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Every blessing</b> in heavenly places is not <b>bank account, job, success</b> - how many Americans talk about blessings</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Louisiana's heavenly\" - \"not when it's 82 degrees at the end of October\"; West Virginia \"almost heaven\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not about <b>Ephesus</b> or their hometown being heavenly</li><li class=\"d0\">Back to <b>holy ones</b> theme</li><li class=\"d1\">part of that status: Father has <b>exalted them to a heavenly position</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>already true</b> of them in some sense - and <b>in Christ</b></li></ul>"},{"t":400.53,"lv":2,"h":"1:4 - \"chose us in him\" - who is \"us\"?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:4</b> chose us in Him <b>before the foundation of the world</b></li><li class=\"d0\">In Galatians kept \"picking on\" <b>Luther</b>; now \"my old friend <b>John Calvin</b>\" for the first couple chapters</li><li class=\"d0\">First read, vaguely familiar with <b>predestination in Calvinism</b>: \"he chose us in him\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Father chose us in Christ before the world was founded</li></ul>"},{"t":452.93,"lv":3,"h":"Who is \"us\" - and who is \"them\"?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">If there's an <b>us</b>, there's a <b>them</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Calvinist reading: us = everyone in history who will have <b>faith</b>; them = everyone who won't</li><li class=\"d1\">anything in Ephesians so far giving those categories? <b>Faith</b> hasn't appeared - <b>faithfulness</b> has</li><li class=\"d1\">\"you're having to <b>create</b> those categories\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Use categories Paul <b>already used</b>: us = <b>the saints</b>, people with that <b>status</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God chose for people to <b>have that status</b></li><li class=\"d1\">them = those who don't (or may not) - \"could be an <b>empty set</b>\"; us \"could be <b>every human</b>\" - Paul doesn't say</li><li class=\"d0\">All we know: us includes <b>Paul and those he writes to</b></li></ul>"},{"t":593.5,"lv":3,"h":"\"Before the foundation of the world\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><i>Foundation</i> = literally a <b>building foundation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Before God the Father chose to <b>create everything</b>, he chose to make <b>us holy ones in the heavenly places</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a specified group of <b>humans</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>purpose</b> - not God musing \"I think I'll create a world\" later</li><li class=\"d1\">these are <b>connected</b> for Paul</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Purpose for which God creates the world = to do this for us</b></li></ul>"},{"t":665.97,"lv":3,"h":"Nothing here about election","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Paul is <b>not defining</b> who is and isn't us - at least <b>not excluding</b> anyone</li><li class=\"d1\">a category of humans - includes Paul and recipients</li><li class=\"d1\">angels? not writing to angels; they're \"already the holy ones of God\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Nothing in here about <b>predestination or election</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">The point: <b>glorification of human persons</b> was the purpose of creation</li><li class=\"d1\">same point as <b>Romans</b>; will say same as <b>Galatians 3</b> -> \"no reason to think this wasn't St. Paul\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>causal</b> point: glorification in Christ, status as holy ones in the heavenly places = purpose for which God <b>laid the foundation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So that we be <b>holy, without blame</b> before him</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>purified of our sins</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>in love</b>\" - sharing his love with us</li></ul>"},{"t":793.85,"lv":2,"h":"1:5 - predestined to adoption as sons","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:5</b> \"having predestined us to <b>adoption as sons</b> by Jesus Christ\" - \"our friend John is getting triggered\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><i>Predestined</i> = <b>set things in order in advance</b>, arranged in advance</li><li class=\"d1\">parallel: creates the world, purpose = glorification of humans -> in creating it he sets everything in order for us to become <b>sons of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sons of God</b> = another OT term for <b>angels</b>, parallel to holy ones</li><li class=\"d0\">\"By Jesus Christ\" = <b>by means of Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> \"sons of Christ\" as distinct from sons of God - <b>sons of God by adoption</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>his sonship</b> is the basis for our adopted sonship</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Good pleasure of his will</b>\" = God desired to do good to us - <b>loves humanity</b></li></ul>"},{"t":944.62,"lv":2,"h":"1:6 - \"glory of his grace\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:6</b> \"to the praise of the glory of his grace, by which he made us accepted in the beloved\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"wonky translation\": \"glory of his grace\" = more like <b>his glorious grace</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Given to us <b>freely</b> - we didn't <b>earn</b> adoption</li><li class=\"d1\">we didn't exist yet when he decided</li><li class=\"d0\">We respond in <b>praise</b> - for creating us, the world, and a <b>destiny</b> set before us in Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">Accepted into God's family <b>in Christ</b> - none of it apart from Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">\"one <b>mediator</b> between God and man, the man Christ Jesus\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Athanasius</b>: God became man so that men might become gods - <b>sons of God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1043.19,"lv":2,"h":"What the verses don't say; theosis","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Every Calvinist he knows can quote these by heart - but <b>nothing</b> about God picking some for heaven and some for hell before creation</li><li class=\"d1\">\"you have to <b>read these categories into the text</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Consistent with <b>Galatians 3</b> and <b>Romans 8</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>sons of God</b>; all creation <b>groaning like a woman about to give birth</b> to produce them</li><li class=\"d1\">\"the purpose of creation\" - \"consistent Pauline theology\"</li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>theosis</b> in the Orthodox Church</li></ul>"},{"t":1118.53,"lv":3,"h":"\"This is who you are in Christ\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Compare <b>1 Corinthians</b>: \"holy ones\" language, but there calling them to <b>repentance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"this is who you are in Christ - start acting like it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Here: laying out the <b>gospel</b> - the status you have in Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">not because, like <b>Julius Caesar</b>, you were so great you experienced <b>apotheosis</b> and became a god</li><li class=\"d1\">God <b>loved you before the world was created</b>, created it to give you this destiny</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>adoption</b>, becoming an <b>heir</b> of his promises</li><li class=\"d0\">Even if you don't look, feel, or act like it any given day</li><li class=\"d1\">\"peasants doing <b>glorified slave labor</b> in a field... in the <b>Lycus Valley</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">a nobody to Rome: <b>slave, woman</b> - what society held no value for</li><li class=\"d1\">\"this is the <b>value God has for you</b>\" - every single one</li></ul>"},{"t":1236.93,"lv":2,"h":"1:7 - Redemption through his blood","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:7</b> \"in him we have <b>redemption through his blood</b>, the forgiveness of sins according to the riches of his grace\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><i>Redemption</i> = <b>to buy back</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like redeeming a coupon or gift certificate - turn it in, get something back</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ offered <b>his blood</b> to get us back - \"offers himself in order to get us back\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1286.61,"lv":3,"h":"Q: \"the beloved\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: odd that he calls Christ \"<b>the beloved</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">v. 4: without blame before him <b>in love</b></li><li class=\"d1\">theme through these nested verses: everything we receive from the Father we receive <b>in and through Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">includes <b>God's love</b> - Christ is \"the <b>Beloved</b>, capital B\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Love between the persons of the <b>Trinity</b> is <b>infinite</b>, back into eternity</li><li class=\"d1\">that love then <b>shared with us</b> as humans</li><li class=\"d1\">adopted sons: God sharing his <b>life and love</b> that eternally existed between the three persons</li></ul>"},{"t":1391.9,"lv":3,"h":"Why blood forgives sins","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Connection between <b>blood</b> and <b>forgiveness</b>? OT sacrifice</li><li class=\"d0\">In sacrifice <b>killing the animal is irrelevant</b>, not ritualized</li><li class=\"d1\">nothing in the <b>Torah</b> on how to kill it</li><li class=\"d1\">sacrifices are <b>sacred meals</b> - involve food; must kill to eat; drain the blood (not eaten)</li><li class=\"d1\">incidental - Torah has instructions on <b>butchering</b>: parts to eat, burn, offer</li><li class=\"d0\">So <b>blood is not a stand-in for death</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"forgiveness because Christ died\" - his death is significant (1 Cor 15) but this is about <b>what was done with the blood</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Blood used to <b>wipe away the taint</b> of sin - purify, cover</li><li class=\"d1\">\"absorb the sin residue, <b>the goo</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Guilt and sin offerings <b>every day</b> - so why a <b>Day of Atonement</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">atoning for <b>physical objects</b> in the tabernacle: sin <b>taints everything around it</b> - ground, world</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>atonement = purification</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. John's epistles</b>: Christ's blood <b>purifying and washing</b> us - washing in blood counterintuitive, but blood purifies</li></ul>"},{"t":1625.47,"lv":3,"h":"Redeemed and purified","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Redeemed</b> = brought back from <b>death</b>; <b>purified</b> of sins through his blood</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Riches of his grace\" - still talking about what <b>God does</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Father: creation for our adoption</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ: <b>redeeming and purifying</b> us - <b>prerequisite</b> to the status and adoption</li></ul>"},{"t":1678.69,"lv":2,"h":"1:8-9 - the mystery made known","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:8-9</b> grace made to abound \"in all wisdom and prudence, having <b>made known to us the mystery of his will</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Plan of redemption, adoption, glorification <b>not on the first page of Scripture</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God doesn't tell <b>Adam</b> \"here's how it'll go down... several millennia\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not laid out to <b>Abraham</b> (broad strokes), <b>Moses</b>, <b>Isaiah</b> - still a <b>mystery</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Made known to us</b> - Paul and recipients, \"not necessarily excluding anybody\"</li><li class=\"d1\">gospel given to Paul, Paul preached it to them, spreading through the world</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The mystery that was true all along\" - same terms: <b>good pleasure</b>, before the foundation</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul sees his <b>Damascus road</b> change as a change in <b>where he is on the timeline</b></li><li class=\"d1\">from expecting it -> <b>it has arrived</b>, revealed</li></ul>"},{"t":1810.74,"lv":2,"h":"1:10 - fullness of the times","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:10</b> \"in the <b>dispensation of the fullness of the times</b>... gather together in one all things in Christ, in heaven and on earth\"</li><li class=\"d0\">The whole <b>purpose of God</b> coming to fulfillment - in his communities, in his gospel</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"a new religion... better than the old one. <b>You can eat pork now</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"no more killing animals... don't have to go to Jerusalem\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul sees a <b>shift in epoch</b>: purpose of all creation being fulfilled</li><li class=\"d1\">\"this is the <b>end times</b>\" - everything coming together in Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">Why reiterate to them? Some are <b>slaves on farms 12-16 hours a day</b>, women, poor, looked down on</li><li class=\"d1\">\"here's where you are in the <b>cosmos</b>\" - God created everything for you because he loves you</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul excluding anyone from \"us\" yet? <b>No</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"no Calvinist version of predestination here\" - no <b>them</b> yet</li></ul>"},{"t":1960.94,"lv":2,"h":"1:11 - an inheritance","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:11</b> \"in him we have obtained an <b>inheritance</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">language of <b>Galatians 3</b> (sons, heir) and <b>Romans 8</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ is the <b>heir</b>, the Son; we've received adopted sonship -> a share in the inheritance <b>in Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Being predestined according to the purpose of him who <b>works all things according to the counsel of his will</b>\" - \"fun with translations\"</li><li class=\"d0\">What's predestined? <b>The inheritance</b> - arranged in advance</li><li class=\"d1\">set up out of <b>love</b>, good will toward us</li></ul>"},{"t":2043.51,"lv":3,"h":"God working - not a puppet master","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Works all things\" - not a <b>blueprint</b> or \"bulletin board with strings and pins\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God <b>active all the way through</b>, from creation until then</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not sitting somewhere planning it out, <b>not puppet master</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Grace = God acting in his creation</b> - all along</li><li class=\"d1\">purpose: <b>glorification</b>, inheritance, adoption, <b>blessing in the heavenly places</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"no one's been excluded\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2118.23,"lv":2,"h":"1:12 - \"who first trusted\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Better: \"we who <b>in the first place trusted</b> in Christ should be to the praise of his glory\"</li><li class=\"d1\">at the beginning we trusted - began a life of <b>faithfulness</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God continues to work to bring it to fruition</li><li class=\"d1\">not just <b>macro</b> level in the cosmos - in <b>your and my life</b>, that peasant's, that slave's</li><li class=\"d1\">from trusting in the gospel to <b>glory</b>, for the praise of God</li><li class=\"d0\">True of <b>Paul and everyone he speaks to</b> - all we get from the text</li><li class=\"d1\">\"doesn't mean it's true of every single human who ever existed\" - not what Paul is talking about</li></ul>"},{"t":2210.34,"lv":2,"h":"1:13 - the gospel of your salvation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:13</b> \"in him you also trusted\" (\"trusted\" in italics) after you heard the <b>word of truth, the gospel of your salvation</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>We</b> who first trusted, now <b>you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God working through <b>Paul</b> (v. 1) to bring the gospel to them</li><li class=\"d0\">The gospel is <b>not</b> \"here's what you need to do to be saved\"</li><li class=\"d1\">in Acts, hearers ask <b>\"What must I do to be saved?\"</b> - would be a dumb question if that was the gospel</li></ul>"},{"t":2284.05,"lv":3,"h":"<i>Evangelion</i> = report of victory","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><i>Evangelion</i> (singular) in NT; Roman world more commonly plural <i>evangelia</i></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>report of victory</b> - military usually - or accomplishments of an <b>emperor, general, senator</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Gospel of your salvation\" = you heard the <b>report of Christ's victory</b> that produced your salvation</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>redemption</b>, <b>forgiveness of sins</b> - what Christ accomplished</li><li class=\"d0\">Heard and trusted -> <b>baptized</b> -> received the <b>Holy Spirit</b>, \"<b>sealed</b> with the Holy Spirit of promise\"</li><li class=\"d1\">still say at <b>chrismation</b>: \"the seal of the gift of the Holy Spirit\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2365.14,"lv":2,"h":"The seal - and Calvin","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">A seal is <b>not shrink wrap</b> - a <b>wax seal</b></li><li class=\"d1\">put your <b>stamp</b> on it: you were stamped, <b>claimed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"I feel disingenuous saying I hate to pick on John Calvin\" - \"but I'm going to\"</li><li class=\"d0\">A wax seal <b>can be broken</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Calvinists: sealed = <b>can never fall away</b>, never lose the Spirit</li><li class=\"d1\">built on misreading of the earlier verses (God picked you rather than others) - \"nowhere in there\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Anyone who knew wax seals knew they break</li><li class=\"d1\">\"the whole point\" = break easily so you could tell if opened</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> permanent or unbreakable</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul could have said \"bound\" or <b>\"an eternal seal... an unbreakable seal\"</b> - he doesn't</li><li class=\"d1\">says neither way; but the <b>wax seal analogy</b> leads one to think it can be broken</li></ul>"},{"t":2514.98,"lv":2,"h":"1:14 - the guarantee is a deposit","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>1:14</b> Holy Spirit \"is the <b>guarantee</b> of our inheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Calvinist friends read a lot into the English <b>\"guarantee\"</b> - a <b>modern</b> definition</li><li class=\"d1\">older sense (NKJV \"not that new\") = <b>deposit</b></li><li class=\"d1\">deposit as evidence you'll pay the rest</li><li class=\"d0\">Holy Spirit = the <b>down payment</b> / <b>deposit</b> of our inheritance</li><li class=\"d1\">until the redemption - \"cash it in\" - of the purchased possession = <b>the inheritance</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Inheritance: adopted sons, <b>glorification</b> in heavenly places</li><li class=\"d1\">down payment = <b>Holy Spirit given at baptism</b>, when you first trusted the gospel of Christ's accomplished salvation</li></ul>"},{"t":2629.87,"lv":2,"h":"The Spirit as the beginning of glorification","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Holy Spirit = God himself</b> indwelling us = the <b>beginning of our glorification, our inheritance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"not a coupon or a ticket\" - a <b>deposit</b>, part of the inheritance</li><li class=\"d1\">we become <b>temple of the Holy Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not saying deposit means you automatically get the whole thing - then no need for a deposit</li><li class=\"d1\">you could <b>default on a loan</b>, <b>lose your deposit</b>, <b>break a seal</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not saying it <b>can</b> be broken - but must say, because of Calvinist friends, he's not saying the <b>opposite</b> either</li><li class=\"d1\">no mention of anyone <b>excluded</b>; no mention of it being <b>unbreakable</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2730.44,"lv":3,"h":"Faithfulness and where he pauses","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">God is working to bring it to a conclusion - nothing about whether <b>we can decide not to</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Back at the start: holy ones <b>faithful</b> to Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">faithful = an <b>ongoing</b> verb and action</li><li class=\"d0\">God started his part <b>before there was a world</b>, for my salvation and yours</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no guarantees about our faithfulness</b> - the other piece; he'll delve into it as we go on</li><li class=\"d0\">Good place to <b>pause</b> though not end of chapter - next verse starts with a \"<b>therefore</b>\"</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next: picking up at the <b>\"therefore\"</b> in the next verse (<b>1:15</b>)"});
